<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="OMS Rust CAL Core Interfaces" id="m-oms-rust-cal-001" version="5.0.0">
  <folder name="Strategy" id="id-fb479a9b615e4ac8bd2e55cbf723ef92" type="strategy"/>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-60eb801611b14da89d6346eb18c91146" type="business"/>
  <folder name="Application" id="f-app" type="application">
    <folder name="Error Handling" id="f-err">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="CalError" id="e-calerror">
        <documentation>Rust equivalent of UCIException. Primary error carrier for all fallible CAL operations. Implements std::error::Error plus Send plus Sync. Fields: kind (CalErrorKind), message (String), source (Option of boxed Error). CERTs: CAL-005204, CAL-005369, CAL-016043. Ref: Section 5.1.2.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="CalErrorKind" id="e-calerror-kind">
        <documentation>Non-exhaustive enum classifying CAL error conditions. Variants: InitializationFailure (CAL-005204), TopicUnavailable (CAL-005369), ResourcesUnavailable (CAL-016043), InvalidState (Table 5.9-2), UuidConformanceError (CAL-016477), OperationNotPermitted (CAL-016050), AsbFailed, InvalidServiceIdentifier, SerializationError, AbstractInstantiation (CAL-016035), ImplementationError.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="CalResult(T)" id="e-calresult">
        <documentation>Type alias: type CalResult(T) = Result(T, CalError). Return type for all fallible CAL operations. Replaces C++ and Java exception propagation. Every operation that can signal a UCIException in C++ returns CalResult(T) in the Rust CAL. Ref: Section 5.1.2.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="UUID" id="f-uuid">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="CalUuid" id="e-caluuid">
        <documentation>RFC 4122 conformant UUID enforced by construction. Newtype wrapper over uuid::Uuid. Validation applied at every construction path. Invariants: Variant = RFC 4122 Leach-Salz (CAL-016479), Version in {1, 3, 4} (CAL-005181). CERTs: CAL-016477, CAL-016479, CAL-005181.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="ServiceUuids" id="e-serviceuuids">
        <documentation>Aggregates UUIDs identifying a CAL Client service context. Fields: system (CalUuid), service (CalUuid), subsystem (Option of CalUuid), components (Vec of CalUuid), capabilities (Vec of CalUuid). Retrieved via AbstractServiceBus::uuids() after initialisation. CERT: CAL-005203.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Accessors" id="f-acc">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="RequiredField(T)" id="e-reqfield">
        <documentation>Trait providing read/write access to a field that is always present (xs:element minOccurs=1 maxOccurs=1). Methods: get() returning reference to T, get_mut() returning mutable reference to T, set(value: T). Ref: Section 5.5.1.2, 5.5.4.2.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="OptionalField(T)" id="e-optfield">
        <documentation>Trait for optionally-populated fields. Created in DISABLED state (CAL-005254). Methods: is_enabled(), get() returning Option, set(value) which enables, disable(). CERTs: CAL-005254, CAL-005290, CAL-005293, CAL-005294, CAL-005296.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="BoundedListField(T)" id="e-bndfield">
        <documentation>Trait for bounded list of homogeneous elements. Created EMPTY (CAL-005264). Methods: len(), is_empty(), max_bound(), min_bound(), reserve(n), push(elem), pop(), clear(), get(i). CERT: CAL-005264.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="ChoiceField(V)" id="e-choicefield">
        <documentation>Trait for discriminated union field. Created UNINITIALIZED (CAL-005267). V is a generated enum with one variant per schema choice alternative. Methods: get(), get_mut(), set(value: V), clear(), is_set(). CERT: CAL-005267.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="CalMessage" id="e-calmessage">
        <documentation>Marker trait for top-level publishable OMS message types. Only CalMessage types may be associated with a topic. Non-abstract messages implement this trait. Abstract message types must not be instantiated (CAL-016035). CERTs: CAL-016033, CAL-016035.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="CalSubMessage" id="e-calsubmessage">
        <documentation>Marker trait for nested sub-message types used as fields within CalMessage types. CalSubMessage instances cannot be sent or received outside the context of an encapsulating CalMessage. Ref: Section 5.5.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Abstract Service Bus" id="f-asb">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="CalInstanceConfig" id="e-calinstanceconfig">
        <documentation>Configuration parameters for initialising a CAL instance. Fields: service_identifier (String, CAL-005201), asb_identifier (String, CAL-005202), network_config_path (PathBuf, Section 4.7). CERTs: CAL-005201, CAL-005202.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="AsbConnectionState" id="e-asbstate">
        <documentation>Enum of ASB connection states per Table 5.9-1: Initializing (optional), Normal (required), Degraded (optional), Inoperable (optional), Failed (required). Provides validate_transition() enforcing the Figure 5.9-2 state machine rules.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="AsbStatus" id="e-asbstatus">
        <documentation>Snapshot of current ASB connection status delivered to registered listeners and returned by polling calls. Fields: state (AsbConnectionState), description (String). Ref: Section 5.9.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="AsbStatusListener" id="e-asblistener">
        <documentation>Trait implemented by CAL Clients to receive ASB connection status change notifications via callback. Method: on_status_change(status: AsbStatus). Called immediately upon registration (CAL-016366), then on every subsequent state change.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="AbstractServiceBus" id="e-asb">
        <documentation>Primary CAL instance interface. Methods: service_id(), uuids() (CAL-005203), connection_status(), register_status_listener() (CAL-016366), unregister_status_listener(), create_writer(), create_reader(). CERTs: CAL-005201, CAL-005202, CAL-005203, CAL-016366.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="CalInstanceFactory" id="e-calfactory">
        <documentation>Platform entry-point function for obtaining a fully initialised CAL instance. Signature: fn(config: CalInstanceConfig) returning CalResult of boxed AbstractServiceBus. CERTs: CAL-005201, CAL-005202.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Technology" id="f-tech" type="technology">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="ASB Network Service" id="e-asbtech">
      <documentation>Technology layer representation of the Abstract Service Bus network service. Realizes the messaging infrastructure used by AbstractServiceBus implementations. Ref: Section 4.12.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Network Configuration" id="e-netconfig">
      <documentation>Configuration artifact specifying valid CAL Topics, network connections, and transport layer mappings for a CAL instance. Ref: Section 4.7.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
